

1. Introduction
TEXT:

This Agreement governs the loan by Goldman Sachs Bank USA (the 'Lender') to Amazon.com, Inc. (the 'Borrower') in the principal amount of $1,000,000,000 (the 'Loan'). The Loan proceeds will be used by the Borrower for general corporate purposes. The Loan will be governed by the laws of the State of New York and will have a term of 5 years. The interest rate on the Loan will be LIBOR + 2.5%. The parties have entered into this Agreement as of January 1, 2023 (the 'Effective Date').

2. Parties
(a) Goldman Sachs Bank USA, a Delaware corporation with its principal place of business at 200 West Street, New York, NY 10282, USA (the 'Lender'), is a financial institution engaged in investment banking, securities trading, and other financial services.

(b) Amazon.com, Inc., a Delaware corporation with its principal place of business at 410 Terry Avenue North, Seattle, WA 98109, USA (the 'Borrower'), is a leading e-commerce company and cloud computing provider.

(c) The Borrower acknowledges that it has the legal capacity to enter into this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder. The Borrower further acknowledges that it has obtained all necessary approvals, authorizations, and consents to enter into this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

(d) The Lender acknowledges that it has the legal capacity to enter into this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder. The Lender further acknowledges that it has obtained all necessary approvals, authorizations, and consents to enter into this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

(e) Each of the parties hereto represents and warrants to the other that it is executing this Agreement as its duly authorized representative.

(f) The Lender and the Borrower may each be referred to herein individually as a 'Party' and collectively as the 'Parties'.

3. Loan Terms
(a) Loan Amount. The Lender agrees to make a loan to the Borrower in the principal amount of $1,000,000,000 (the 'Loan').

(b) Loan Term. The term of the Loan will be five (5) years from the Effective Date (the 'Loan Term').

(c) Interest Rate. The interest rate on the Loan will be the London Interbank Offered Rate ('LIBOR') as published by the British Bankers' Association or any successor publication, plus 2.5% (the 'Marginal').

(d) Loan Purpose. The Borrower will use the Loan proceeds for general corporate purposes.

(e) Repayment. The Borrower will repay the Loan in full, including accrued interest, on the last day of the Loan Term. The Borrower may prepay the Loan in whole or in part at any time without penalty.

(f) Security. The Borrower grants the Lender a security interest in the Collateral (as defined in Section 4 below) to secure the Loan.

(g) Default. If the Borrower defaults on any of its obligations under this Agreement, the Lender may exercise its rights and remedies under this Agreement and applicable law, including foreclosing on the Collateral.

(h) Amendment. This Agreement may be amended only by a written instrument executed by both Parties.

(i) Governing Law. This Agreement will be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York.

(j) Entire Agreement. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties and supersedes all prior negotiations, understandings, and agreements between the Parties, whether written or oral, relating to the subject matter hereof.

(k) Counterparts. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which will be deemed an original, but all of which together will constitute one and the same instrument.

(l) Binding Effect. This Agreement will be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the Parties and their respective successors and assigns.

(m) Notices. All notices, requests, demands, and other communications under this Agreement will be in writing and will be deemed duly given when delivered in person or sent by registered or certified mail, return receipt requested, postage prepaid, or by facsimile or email (with confirmation of transmission), to the respective addresses set forth in the Contact Information section above or to such other address as a Party may designate by notice to the other Party in accordance with this Section.

(n) Waiver. No failure or delay by a Party in exercising any right, power, or privilege under this Agreement will operate as a waiver of such right, power, or privilege, nor will any single exercise of any right, power, or privilege preclude any other or further exercise of any right, power, or privilege.

(o) Severability. If any provision of this Agreement is held to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable in any respect, such provision will be ineffective only to the extent of such invalidity, illegality, or unenforceability, without affecting the validity, legality, or enforceability of the remaining provisions.

(p) Headings. The headings in this Agreement are for convenience only and will not affect the interpretation of this Agreement.

(q) Counterparts/Electronic Signatures. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which will be deemed an original, but all of which together will constitute one and the same instrument. The parties agree to the use of electronic signatures, and any signature delivered by electronic means (including portable document format (PDF) or any other electronic means) will be of the same legal effect, validity, and enforceability as an original signature delivered in writing.

(r) Governing Language. In the event of a conflict between the English and any other language version of this Agreement, the English version will control.

