5. Representations and Warranties
The Borrower represents and warrants to the Lender as follows:

5.1 Authority

The Borrower has full power and authority to execute and deliver this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder. This Agreement has been duly executed and delivered by the Borrower and constitutes the legal, valid, and binding obligation of the Borrower, enforceable against the Borrower in accordance with its terms, except as limited by applicable bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, moratorium, or similar laws affecting creditors' rights generally and general principles of equity.

5.2 Security

The Borrower owns the Collateral, free and clear of any liens, encumbrances, or other security interests, except for any liens, encumbrances, or other security interests that have been waived in writing by the holders thereof and delivered to the Lender.

5.3 Loan Proceeds

The Loan Proceeds will be used by the Borrower solely for the purpose of general corporate purposes, and the Borrower will not use the Loan Proceeds for any other purpose without the prior written consent of the Lender.

The Lender makes no representation or warranty, express or implied, with respect to the Loan or the Borrower, except as expressly set forth in this Agreement. The Lender relies solely on the representations and warranties made by the Borrower in this Agreement.

The Borrower acknowledges and agrees that it has not relied on any representations or warranties made by the Lender, except as expressly set forth in this Agreement.

6. Interest and Fees
6.1 Interest

The Borrower shall pay interest on the Loan at a rate equal to the London Interbank Offered Rate ('LIBOR') as published by the British Bankers' Association ('BBA') for the London Interbank Market for US Dollar deposits with a maturity of one month, plus a margin of 2.5% (the 'Marginal Rate'). The interest shall be calculated on the daily unpaid principal balance of the Loan and shall be payable monthly in arrears.

6.2 Fees

The Borrower shall pay all fees and expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the Loan, including but not limited to, legal fees, document preparation fees, and other expenses, which shall be invoiced to the Borrower by the Lender.

6.3 Late Payment

If any payment of interest or principal is not made when due, the Borrower shall pay a late fee equal to the greater of (i) 5% per annum of the amount due or (ii) the maximum amount allowed by applicable law.

6.4 Prepayment

The Borrower may prepay all or any portion of the Loan at any time without penalty, provided that the Borrower pays all accrued and unpaid interest on the prepaid amount.

7. Default and Remedies
TEXT:
7. Default and Remedies

7.1 Default

The Borrower shall be in default under this Agreement if any of the following events occur:

(a) The Borrower fails to make any payment when due, including principal, interest, and fees;

(b) The Borrower breaches any representation or warranty made in this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within 30 days after receiving written notice from the Lender;

(c) The Borrower files a petition for voluntary or involuntary bankruptcy or any other insolvency proceeding;

(d) The Borrower makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors; or

(e) The Borrower disposes of, encumbers, or otherwise transfers any of the security provided under this Agreement without the prior written consent of the Lender.

7.2 Acceleration

Upon the occurrence of an event of default, the Lender shall have the right to declare all amounts then outstanding under this Agreement immediately due and payable.

7.3 Remedies

In the event of a default, the Lender shall have the right to exercise any or all of the following remedies:

(a) To take possession of the security provided under this Agreement;

(b) To sell, assign, or otherwise dispose of the security, either as a whole or in parcels, at public or private sale, for cash, credit, or on terms and conditions deemed appropriate by the Lender;

(c) To apply the proceeds of any sale, assignment, or disposition of the security to the payment of the amounts outstanding under this Agreement, including principal, interest, fees, and expenses; and

(d) To take any other action permitted by law or under the terms of this Agreement to protect its interests.

7.4 Waiver

The Lender's failure to exercise or delay in exercising any right or remedy under this Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of such right or remedy. Any waiver by the Lender of any default under this Agreement must be in writing and signed by an authorized officer of the Lender.

7.5 Subordination

The Borrower acknowledges and agrees that the security provided under this Agreement shall be subordinate to all liens, claims, and encumbrances created by the Borrower in favor of third parties securing indebtedness incurred by the Borrower for the purpose of carrying on its business, except as otherwise agreed in writing by the Lender.

7.6 Further Assurances

The Borrower shall execute and deliver, at the Lender's request and expense, all such further instruments and documents and take all such further action as the Lender may reasonably require to carry out the provisions of this Agreement and to assure the Lender of its rights and remedies under this Agreement.

7.7 Applicable Law

The rights and remedies of the Lender under this Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York.

